<title>UK: Aluminium output rose in May - IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium output rose in May - IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily average primary aluminium output in May rose to 52,900 tonnes compared with 52,800 in April and 50,800 in May 1996, provisional figures from the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) show.</p>
<p>Total production in May (31 days) was 1.640 million tonnes, compared with 1.584 million in April (30 days) and 1.574 million in May 1996.  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of primary aluminium production was as follows (in thousands of tonnes) the IPAI said.</p>
<p>			May 97    Apr 97    May 96</p>
<p>Africa		    93     91	  86</p>
<p>N.America		502    485	 498</p>
<p>S.America		180    175	 177</p>
<p>East/South Asia	162    156	 134</p>
<p>Europe West	    277    266	 269</p>
<p>Europe East/Central  282    272	 271</p>
<p>Oceania		  144    139	 139</p>
</text>
